# Product Principles / プロダクト原則

## Core Positioning / コアポジショニング

Regapro AI is a **business OS** (ビジネス OS) — not an AI chat app, not a dashboard toy, and not a collection of disconnected AI features.

- Users come to **do work** (案件、顧客、タスク、調査、成果物の作成・更新).
- AI is an **embedded capability** within work flows, never the primary surface.
- Every screen must answer: *「今、何の仕事を進めているか？」*

## Organize by Work Units / 作業単位で整理する

Structure navigation, routes, and copy around **user work units** (作業単位), not internal feature names or engineering module names.

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| 案件一覧、今日のタスク、顧客対応 | Repository、Provider、Worker という語を UI に出す |
| 調査 → 下書き → 成果物 | Chat、RAG、Pipeline など実装用語をメニュー名にする |

Internal names (`SearXNGProvider`, `ArtifactService`, `TaskRepository`) belong in code and architecture docs only.

## User-Facing Language / ユーザー向け言語

- Use domain language the user already knows: 案件、顧客、タスク、議事録、提案書、調査メモ.
- Hide implementation details: no "LLM", "embedding", "vector store" in general UI unless the user is a power user in settings.
- Error messages describe **what to do next**, not stack traces or provider names.

## What We Are Not Building / 作らないもの

These are explicit anti-patterns for product framing:

- A full-screen chat with sidebar features bolted on.
- "Ask AI anything" as the home screen.
- Feature grids marketed as "AI capabilities".
- Giant KPI cards and vanity metrics on landing views.
- Marketing-style hero titles with long descriptive paragraphs on every page.

## Quality Bar / 品質基準

Before marking work complete, all of these must pass:

```bash
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm run test
npm run build
```

Maintain strict TypeScript; avoid casual `any`. Prefer explicit domain types and validated boundaries at the Application Service layer.
